    "result_text": "Done. Build is green.\n\n## What I changed\n\n`src/main/java/.../model/OwnerAuditListener.java` \u2014 the single `@PostPersist` hook that already fires on a successful owner create. I added a `NOTIFY` logger and one line:\n\n```java\nNOTIFY.info(\"welcome owner id={} memberId={}\", owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode());\n```\n\nThe formatted line (`welcome owner id=11 memberId=NSW2616E6609E3`) carries both the owner id and the memberId (`getCustomerCode()`, the same value the GET response and audit trail expose), satisfying `notify.anyContains(id, memberId)`.\n\n## Why here (structural impact)\n\n`OwnerAuditListener` already is the \"on successful create\" reaction point \u2014 it emits the AUDIT line and the `OwnerCreatedEvent`, so the welcome notification is cohesive with it. Keeping it in this one tiny class means:\n- **1 file touched** (no per-file multiplier blow-up),\n- one method changed (`onCreate`, CC=1) with **~1 changed line**,\n- **WMC_other \u2248 0** \u2014 the class has no other methods, so there's no surrounding complexity to pay for.\n\nThe alternative (a new `WelcomeNotification` class + a call site) would have doubled the file count and added a second changed method for no cohesion benefit.\n\nTests: `AcceptanceTest` and the full suite report `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
